    <!-- 02 / Founder problem -->
    <section class="bf-section bf-problem" aria-labelledby="bf-problem-title">
      <div class="bf-wrap">
        <div class="bf-problem-head">
          <div>
            <p class="bf-eyebrow">THE FOUNDER'S PROBLEM</p>
            <h2 class="bf-heading" id="bf-problem-title">Your product is clear to you. <em>Is it clear to someone comparing options?</em></h2>
          </div>
          <p class="bf-intro">
            Buyers do not make decisions from your feature list alone. They compare alternatives, test product fit, question claims and look for reasons to trust one solution over another. Your content should help them do that.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bf-problem-grid">
          <article class="bf-problem-card">
            <span class="bf-number">01 / PRODUCT VALUE</span>
            <h3>Your differentiation gets lost in the detail.</h3>
            <p>You know what the product does. Translating its real value into language buyers recognise is a different task.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="bf-problem-card">
            <span class="bf-number">02 / BUYER COMPARISON</span>
            <h3>Prospects are comparing. Your product is missing from the conversation.</h3>
            <p>Buyers are researching competitors and alternatives before they speak to you. You need useful pages for those moments.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="bf-problem-card">
            <span class="bf-number">03 / CONTENT GAP</span>
            <h3>Your content explains. It does not always help people choose.</h3>
            <p>Category education has a role. But buyers also need product-level answers, evidence and meaningful comparisons.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="bf-problem-card">
            <span class="bf-number">04 / FOUNDER CAPACITY</span>
            <h3>You cannot own every part of marketing yourself.</h3>
            <p>Product, customers and sales already compete for your attention. Specialist research and writing need focused ownership.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 / Deliverables -->
