    <!-- 04 / Method -->
    <section class="bf-section bf-method" aria-labelledby="bf-method-title">
      <div class="bf-wrap bf-method-layout">
        <div class="bf-method-aside">
          <p class="bf-eyebrow">HOW I APPROACH THE WORK</p>
          <h2 class="bf-heading" id="bf-method-title">Before I write about your product, <em>I need to understand it.</em></h2>
          <p class="bf-intro">
            I don't start with a keyword list and fill in the blanks. I start with the product, the buyer and the decision the content needs to help with.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bf-method-list">
          <article class="bf-method-step">
            <span class="bf-method-index">01</span>
            <div><h3>Understand the buyer and positioning</h3><p>Review who the product serves, the problem it solves, existing positioning and the evidence behind its claims. Refine unclear inputs where needed.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="bf-method-step">
            <span class="bf-method-index">02</span>
            <div><h3>Map the buying decision</h3><p>Research buyer problems, use cases, evaluation criteria, objections, competing options and the questions that signal genuine intent.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="bf-method-step">
            <span class="bf-method-index">03</span>
            <div><h3>Get inside the product</h3><p>Study documentation, workflows and real use cases. Speak with you or the people who know the product so the content reflects what it can—and cannot—do.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="bf-method-step">
            <span class="bf-method-index">04</span>
            <div><h3>Find the angle and build the narrative</h3><p>Connect credible product strengths to what buyers care about. Decide what needs explaining, what evidence supports it and what the reader should understand.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="bf-method-step">
            <span class="bf-method-index">05</span>
            <div><h3>Research, write and edit</h3><p>Build the agreed asset around search intent, product accuracy and the buyer's decision context. The result should be useful, clear and properly supported.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="bf-method-step">
            <span class="bf-method-index">06</span>
            <div><h3>Review and improve</h3><p>Where analytics access permits, review relevant search visibility, engagement, conversions and pipeline influence. Use observed evidence—not assumptions—to decide what to improve.</p></div>
          </article>
          <div class="bf-method-closer">The point isn't to make your product sound impressive. It's to make its real value easier for the right buyer to understand.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 / Why Vevnit -->
